<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cerignola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">28 April 1503</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-war-of-1499-1504">Italian War of 1499–1504</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cerignola was fought on 28 April 1503 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. A Spanish army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-fernandez-de-cordoba">Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba</a> defeated the French under the Duke of Nemours, who was killed. Spanish arquebusiers firing from behind a ditch and rampart broke the French attacks, and it is often counted as the first battle won by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> small arms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cerignola.jpg" alt="Battle of Cerignola" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Federico de Madrazo y Kuntz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elgrancapitantrasbatalladeceri%C3%B1ola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
